# Project Skills and Agents

Use project skills under `.cursor/skills/` and agents under `.cursor/agents/` when the task matches.

## Skills

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `clean-code-review` | Reviewing diffs/PRs, “check clean code”, post-change quality pass |
| `cpeye-feature` | Adding metrics, alerts, settings fields, SMS, reports, scheduler behavior |
| `api-route-authoring` | Creating or editing `src/app/api/**/route.ts` |

## Subagents

| Agent | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `clean-code-reviewer` | Dedicated Clean Code review; use proactively after non-trivial edits |
| `cpeye-domain` | CPE protocol, scheduler, alerts, SMS, reports domain questions or designs |
| `security-auditor` | Auth, JWT, env secrets, SQL injection, credential handling audits |

## Priority

1. Respect always-applied rules (`clean-code`, `cpeye-architecture`, `security`)
2. Load the matching skill workflow before large edits
3. Prefer domain agent for CPE/scheduler design; security agent for auth/secret changes
4. Do not invent Neon/HeroUI/Vercel serverless assumptions — follow architecture rule
